## MEDIUM SEVERITY ISSUES

### ISSUE 9 — Widget JS: `loadChart()` response is parsed incorrectly — chart never renders

**File:** `extensions/size-chart-widget/blocks/size-chart.liquid` lines 1207–1228

The API returns:
```json
{ "id": "...", "name": "...", "category": "...", "type": "...", "data": { "headers": [...], "units": {...}, "rows": [...] } }
```

At line 1221, the widget checks `resp.data.headers` — correct. But at line 1226:
```javascript
var data = Object.assign({ id: resp.id, name: resp.name, category: resp.category }, nested);
```
`nested` is `resp.data` (the inner object with `headers`, `units`, `rows`). After `Object.assign`, `data.headers` exists. But then `renderTable` is called with `data` and iterates `data.rows` using `data.headers` as column keys. The rows in the DB are keyed by the **header string** exactly (e.g., `"Chest"` not `"chest"`). If the header capitalisation changes, `row[h]` will return `undefined` silently. This is a latent bug, not broken today, but fragile.

More critically: at line 1201, `trackEvent('view', { sizeChartId: data.id })` is called, but `data.id` comes from `resp.id` — this is fine.

**Real bug:** The `loadInline()` function at line 1533 checks `!resp.data || !resp.data.headers` — correct. But `showTable()` at line 1181 re-fetches from `resp.data` without checking `resp.error` first. If the API returns `{ "error": "Chart not found" }` with a 404, `resp` is `null` (because `apiFetch` returns `null` for non-ok responses), so the `!resp` check at line 1209 catches it. This is correct. No bug here.

**Actual bug in `loadInline()`:** Line 1532 does `if (loading) loading.style.display = 'none';` but uses `style.display` (not the `hidden` attribute), inconsistent with all other show/hide code. This means if the loading spinner is ever re-shown by toggling the `hidden` attribute, the `style.display = 'none'` will override it and the spinner will stay hidden. Minor inconsistency.

### ISSUE 10 — `api.size-chart.tsx`: No OPTIONS handler for `GET` preflight on cross-origin requests

**File:** `app/routes/api.size-chart.tsx` line 58

The route handles `OPTIONS` in the `loader` function. In React Router 7, the framework may route `OPTIONS` requests to the `action` function (for non-GET methods) or the `loader` (for GET). Since this route has no `action` export, `OPTIONS` preflight requests will hit the loader — which is correct. This is fine as-is.

However, the `api.widget-config.tsx` route also only has a `loader` and handles `OPTIONS` there correctly. This is consistent.

### ISSUE 11 — Side-tab trigger: `position: fixed` is broken on iOS Safari with `overflow: hidden` on parent

**File:** `extensions/size-chart-widget/blocks/size-chart.liquid` lines 355–379 (`.scr-tab-trigger` CSS)

The side tab uses `position: fixed`. iOS Safari ignores `position: fixed` on elements inside a scrollable container or a container with `transform`, `filter`, or `will-change` applied. Many Shopify themes (e.g., Dawn) apply `transform: translateX()` to the main content during cart drawer open. When this happens, the tab trigger disappears or jumps to a wrong position.

**Fix:** The modal is already moved to `document.body` (line 1020). The same should be done for the side tab trigger. Move it to body via JS after creation when `style === 'tab'`:
```javascript
// in renderTrigger(), after the tab branch:
if (style === 'tab') {
  btn = document.createElement('button');
  // ...existing code...
  document.body.appendChild(btn); // append to body, not triggerWrap
  return; // don't append to triggerWrap
}
```

### ISSUE 12 — Modal close button: width/height 36px but min-height/min-width 44px — touch target visual mismatch

**File:** `extensions/size-chart-widget/blocks/size-chart.liquid` lines 458–466

```css
.scr-modal-close {
  width: 36px;
  height: 36px;
  min-height: 44px;
  min-width: 44px;
```

The element has `width: 36px; height: 36px` which overrides the `min-height`/`min-width` when inside a flex container with `flex-shrink: 0` set implicitly. The actual rendered size will be 36×36px, failing the 44×44px WCAG touch target requirement on iOS Safari.

**Fix:** Remove `width` and `height`, keep only `min-width` and `min-height`:
```css
.scr-modal-close {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-height: 44px;
  min-width: 44px;
  /* remove: width: 36px; height: 36px; */
```

### ISSUE 13 — Unit toggle buttons: `min-height: 32px` — fails 44px touch target requirement

**File:** `extensions/size-chart-widget/blocks/size-chart.liquid` lines 539–549

```css
.scr-unit-btn {
  min-height: 32px;
  min-width: 44px;
```

The `min-height` is 32px, below the 44px WCAG 2.1 AA touch target minimum. On iOS Safari, users with larger fingers will frequently mis-tap between "in" and "cm".

**Fix:** Change `min-height: 32px` to `min-height: 44px`.

### ISSUE 14 — `size-recommender.liquid`: radio label `min-height: 40px` — below 44px minimum

**File:** `extensions/size-chart-widget/blocks/size-recommender.liquid` line 301

```css
.scrr-radio-label {
  min-height: 40px;
```

