## LOW SEVERITY ISSUES

### ISSUE 18 — `size-chart.liquid`: `max-height: 92dvh` with `92vh` fallback order is wrong

**File:** `extensions/size-chart-widget/blocks/size-chart.liquid` lines 424–425

```css
max-height: 92dvh;
max-height: 92vh;
```

`dvh` (dynamic viewport height) is the modern unit that accounts for iOS Safari's retractable toolbar. The correct order for progressive enhancement is fallback first, override second:
```css
max-height: 92vh;     /* older browsers */
max-height: 92dvh;    /* modern browsers — overrides above */
```

Currently it's reversed: the `92dvh` line is written first, then overridden by `92vh` for all browsers. This means the `dvh` fix never applies and the modal will clip behind the iOS Safari bottom toolbar.

**Fix — swap the two lines** (line 424 and 425 of `size-chart.liquid`).

### ISSUE 19 — `size-recommender.liquid`: `scrr-powered-link` missing `aria-label` for screen readers

**File:** `extensions/size-chart-widget/blocks/size-recommender.liquid` lines 183–188

The footer link in `size-recommender.liquid` has no `aria-label`, unlike the equivalent link in `size-chart.liquid` (line 279 which has `aria-label="Size Chart & Recommender app"`). A screen reader will read the raw link text "Size Chart & Recommender" which is fine, but the `&amp;` entity will be read literally as "ampersand" in some screen readers.

**Fix:** Add `aria-label` to the link:
```html
<a
  href="https://apps.shopify.com/size-chart-recommender"
  class="scrr-powered-link"
  target="_blank"
  rel="noopener noreferrer"
  aria-label="Size Chart and Recommender app"
>Size Chart &amp; Recommender</a>
```

